skill: "campaign-and-launch-planning"
sections[10]:
  - "\n"
  - "# campaign-and-launch-planning\n\nA **strategy/orchestration skill** — plan the time-boxed campaign (goal, phases, week-by-week map, the brief,\nthe posts) and let **WoopSocial schedule + publish the coordinated social posts** on the timeline. The agent\n**plans + writes + schedules the social side**; the **waitlist/hub, email, ads, checkout, press, and\nlivestream are external/native.**\n\n"
  - "## The POV: the spotlight event, told as one story\nYour content calendar **keeps the lights on**; a **campaign is the spotlight event** — time-boxed, toward\n**one goal**, across **three phases (tease → launch → sustain)** told as **ONE story**, not three\ndisconnected campaigns. Three forces win it: **anticipation** (a waitlist/emotional investment turns launch\nday into a confirmation — launches with real pre-launch marketing see ~30% higher day-one sales; Waitlister,\nvendor-directional), **velocity** (a concentrated coordinated push\nbeats a slow drip — algorithms reward it), and **proof** (post-launch is where you compound trust or confirm\nit was noise). WoopSocial's role is the thing a launch needs most: **coordinated multi-platform publishing**\non the timeline.\n\n"
  - "## Read these first\n1. **brand-profile** — audience/voice.\n2. **goals-and-kpis** — the one primary goal + success metric.\n\n"
  - "## The framework: STORY\n(Depth: `references/the-story-framework.md`.)\n- **S — Set one goal + the brief:** one goal/metric; launch type (soft/hard/phased); 1–3 platforms; the\n  one-page launch brief; discipline over speed.\n- **T — Tease to build demand:** waitlist (specific promise; pre-launch ≈ +30% day-one, vendor) + referral;\n  one campaign hub;\n  BTS/teasers/proof drops; beta group; personalized press/creator outreach (not a mass release).\n- **O — One coordinated launch:** concentrated cross-platform push (velocity rewarded); one CTA + remove\n  friction; **credible urgency** (real scarcity/bonus/deadline — never fake/resetting timers); drop/\n  countdown/live.\n- **R — Reinforce with proof:** testimonials/UGC/demos/objection-answers; sustain (don't go quiet); close\n  the signed-up → used gap.\n- **Y — Yield: measure + debrief:** numbers vs targets per channel; debrief; feed the next campaign; never\n  fabricate.\n\n"
  - "## The reality (verify-quarterly)\nCampaign-as-spotlight + the three-phase funnel as one story; pre-launch (anticipation/emotional investment,\nwaitlist + referral (pre-launch ≈ +30% day-one, vendor), one hub, BTS/proof drops, beta, personalized\npress/creator outreach);\nlaunch (velocity rewarded, one CTA, credible urgency — no fake timers, drop/countdown/live); post-launch\n(proof, sustain, signed-up→used gap); launch types (soft/hard/phased); orchestration (1–3 platforms,\nrepurpose-not-copy, hero posts/phase, parallel email sequence); planning discipline (one-page brief,\nreadiness, week-by-week map): `references/launch-2026-reality.md`. The brief + week-by-week map + phase×\nplatform grid + urgency mechanics + worked examples: `references/launch-plan-and-recipes.md`.\n\n"
  - "## Honest scope (never violate)\n- **The agent** plans the campaign + writes the **brief**, the **week-by-week map**, and the **posts**, and\n  designs the phases/urgency/hero moments.\n- **WoopSocial schedules + publishes the coordinated social posts** on the timeline (`SCHEDULE_FOR_LATER` +\n  per-platform fields; validate via `platform-specs-and-validation`). It does **not** host the **waitlist/\n  landing-page/hub**, send the **email sequence** (an ESP does), process **checkout/the sale**, run **paid\n  ads**, do **press/creator outreach** (human/DM), run the **livestream** (native), or measure **conversions/\n  ROI** (native analytics + the store).\n- **Credible urgency only** (no fake/resetting countdowns or invented scarcity/signup counts); **never\n  fabricate** anticipation or results; **coordinate, don't spam.** (Scope, distinctions + connections:\n  `references/scope-and-connections.md`.)\n\n"
  - "## Distinct from its siblings (route correctly)\n**campaign-and-launch-planning (this)** = the time-boxed spotlight campaign (phases toward one goal) ·\n**content-calendar** = the ongoing always-on cadence · **goals-and-kpis** = the targets a campaign serves ·\n**collabs-and-cross-promotion** / **lead-magnets-and-funnels** / **email-and-newsletter** /\n**link-in-bio-and-traffic** / **livestream-and-realtime** / **ugc-and-influencer** = the pieces a launch\norchestrates.\n\n"
  - "## Where this connects\nReads first: **brand-profile**, **goals-and-kpis**, **competitor-analysis**. Orchestrates:\n**lead-magnets-and-funnels**/**link-in-bio-and-traffic** (the hub/waitlist), **email-and-newsletter** (the\nparallel sequence), **collabs-and-cross-promotion**/**ugc-and-influencer** (press/creator/partner moments),\n**livestream-and-realtime** (the live), the **format skills** + **thumbnail-design** (assets),\n**cross-platform-repurposing** (one asset → many cuts). Publishes via: **scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial**\n(the coordinated timeline) + **platform-specs-and-validation**; **content-calendar** reserves the slots.\nMeasures with: **analytics-and-reporting** + the store. Hub, email, ads, checkout, press, live + conversion\nmeasurement stay external/native.\n\n"
  - "## Definition of done\nOne primary goal + metric set and a one-page launch brief written; a launch type chosen and 1–3 platforms\npicked; the three-phase arc designed as one story with a week-by-week map and 1–2 hero moments per phase; a\nwaitlist/hub + referral and BTS/proof/press in pre-launch; a coordinated launch-day push behind one CTA with\ncredible urgency; a post-launch proof + sustain plan that closes the signed-up→used gap; per-channel numbers\nread against targets; the social posts scheduled/published via WoopSocial while the hub, email, ads, checkout,\npress, live, and conversion measurement stay external/native; nothing fabricated and no fake urgency;\ncorrectly distinguished from content-calendar and goals-and-kpis.\n"
